-* Throws `\InvalidArgumentException` if `$length` is negative.
+* Reads at most `max(1, $length)` source elements before the first output and buffers at most `$length` values, so it is suitable for long or infinite inputs.
+* While suspended at an output, the source is not advanced until the consumer advances.
+* Validation is lazy: a negative `$length` throws `\InvalidArgumentException` when iteration starts, before touching the source. Constructing the generator does not consume the source.
 
